# Scripts with credentials (use *.example as templates)
# POLICY: these are ignored because they EMBED credentials or fleet IPs, not because
# they are scripts. Audited 2026-08-11 against the known secret values: 10 of 14 hit,
# so this list is doing real work -- do not bulk-un-ignore it.
# A script that sources its secrets instead (e.g. /etc/ktp/discord-relay.conf, as
# scripts/ktp-hltv-liveness.sh does) carries nothing sensitive and SHOULD be tracked.
# That refactor is the way to shrink this list; deleting lines from it is not.
# ⚠️ A keyword grep is not sufficient to clear a file: hltv-api.py was called clean
# twice before a value-based check found AUTH_KEY on line 34. Match the VALUES.
scripts/ktp-scheduled-restart.sh
scripts/ktp-organize-hltv-demos.sh
scripts/hltv-api.py
scripts/ktp-backup.sh
scripts/audit-fleet.json
scripts/audit_fleet_versions.py
scripts/verify_new_staged.py
# RETIRED 2026-08-17, and listed here on purpose rather than left unmentioned. It embeds a
# live Discord webhook, and it was neither tracked nor ignored -- so nothing had decided it
# should stay out of git, and a `git add` from a data-server checkout would have published
# the webhook. ktp-systemd-alert.py supersedes it (relay creds from
# /etc/ktp/discord-relay.conf at runtime); the last two units moved off it on 2026-08-17,
# so nothing invokes it. Correct end state is DELETED from the data server with the webhook
# revoked in Discord -- not tracked, and not copied back in.
# scripts/discord-alert.sh  # removed 2026-08-18: file no longer exists (rule was vestigial)

